  "body": "Second slice of #370 (and part of #361): auto-aligning a vendor STEP by its ISO 13399 tool coordinate systems.\n\n## What changed\n- `ToolCsysReport::align_tool_body()` extracts the tool axis and tip offset (`-dot(origin, axis)`) strictly from CIP (coordinate system in process, ISO 13399-303 §3.3) so that the cutting reference point sits at Z = 0 in the tool frame, pointing up into the spindle along +Z. No fallback to CSIF is performed since CSIF denotes the mounting interface, not the cutting point; missing, ambiguous, or degenerate CIP refuses by name.\n- `ToolBodySpec::from_step_auto(&path)` reads both mesh facets and coordinate systems from a vendor STEP file, aligning it with zero manual offsets. Stated non-mm length units (e.g. inches, cm) are normalized consistently across both geometry and coordinate systems via `step_units::mm_per_unit`.\n- `SetToolBody::from_step_auto(&world, tool_name, &path)` attaches the auto-aligned tool body as one undoable command.\n- `tool_body_view::load_aligned(&path)` returns `LoadedBody` carrying the auto-alignment result or fallback reason, preserving `load` backwards compatibility.\n- In the tool editor (`ToolBodyUi`), importing a STEP file with ISO 13399 coordinate systems automatically sets the axis and tip offset with the note \"aligned by ISO 13399 coordinate systems\"; importing a file without them or with degenerate/ambiguous coordinate systems falls back to default numeric placement ([0, 0, 1] axis, 0 offset) with a note naming why.\n- Manually editing the axis combo or tip offset in the UI clears the alignment note to avoid displaying stale provenance.\n- Test fixture `testdata/models/tool_csys_box_iso13399.step` combining a B-rep box and ISO 13399 placements.\n- `docs/decisions/370-tool-csys-align.md`.\n\nMerged `upstream/main` and clean.\n\n## Readings\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tool_csys`: 11/11 pass.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tool_body`: 12/12 pass.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib tool_body`: 12/12 pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n- `iso_13399_tool_csys_aligns_automatically`\n- `a_file_without_tool_csys_falls_back_by_name`\n- `degenerate_tool_csys_falls_back_by_name`\n- `cip_degenerate_with_csif_valid_must_refuse`\n- `origins_and_facets_in_non_mm_units`\n- `step_with_tool_coordinate_systems_aligns_automatically`\n- `step_without_tool_coordinate_systems_falls_back_by_name`\n- `step_with_degenerate_coordinate_systems_falls_back_by_name`\n- `tool_body_view_load_aligned_handles_step_csys_and_fallback`\n- `import_tool_body_from_step_auto_aligns_in_editor`\n- `import_tool_body_from_step_without_csys_falls_back_by_name_in_editor`\n- `manual_axis_edit_clears_align_note`\n- `pick_tip_sets_manual_placement_note`\n\nChangelog: Tool bodies: align a vendor STEP by its ISO 13399 tool coordinate systems (#370)\n\nFixes #370",
